1
00:00:07,590 --> 00:00:09,133
- There you go.
- Thank you.

2
00:00:23,356 --> 00:00:24,524
Hey.
Can I help you?

3
00:00:26,317 --> 00:00:27,360
Yeah.

4
00:00:28,110 --> 00:00:29,654
He says his name's
Patrick Jane.

5
00:00:30,112 --> 00:00:32,615
- Patrick Jane? Really?
- Red John, right?

6
00:00:33,074 --> 00:00:34,617
Wife and daughter?
About a year ago?

7
00:00:34,784 --> 00:00:36,202
Yeah, he's been
off the radar.

8
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:38,663
Sac P.D. lost track of him
six months ago.

9
00:00:39,705 --> 00:00:40,748
I've never met him.

10
00:00:40,998 --> 00:00:43,417
- Did he say why he came in?
- Just that he wants to talk to you.

11
00:00:44,377 --> 00:00:46,921
Boss, Nevada county
sheriff's office called.

12
00:00:47,046 --> 00:00:49,465
They got a body.
Country road near Malakoff Diggins.

13
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:51,425
You and Cho check it out.
I'll catch up.

14
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:08,317
Mr. Jane, I'm Agent Teresa Lisbon.
You wanted to talk to me?

15
00:01:09,026 --> 00:01:10,069
Hi.

16
00:01:10,987 --> 00:01:12,113
- Hi.
- Um...

17
00:01:14,657 --> 00:01:17,368
Detective Elliott said
that you're in charge of the...

18
00:01:18,077 --> 00:01:19,787
the Red John investigation?

19
00:01:20,162 --> 00:01:21,205
That's right.

20
00:01:21,330 --> 00:01:23,457
We took the case over
from Sac P.D. in May.

21
00:01:24,166 --> 00:01:25,585
What's happening
with the investigation?

22
00:01:26,669 --> 00:01:29,755
That's a big question, Mr. Jane
and we're a little busy right now.

23
00:01:29,922 --> 00:01:31,007
Another case has come in.

24
00:01:31,132 --> 00:01:32,425
Could you come back
another time?

25
00:01:32,967 --> 00:01:35,469
Yeah, well, I can wait.
I-I-I'll wait.

26
00:01:35,678 --> 00:01:38,806
That's not really practical. We don't
have a waiting area for guests.

27
00:01:39,432 --> 00:01:40,933
I could just sit right there.

28
00:01:41,225 --> 00:01:42,685
I'm sorry. It's policy.

29
00:01:43,394 --> 00:01:44,437
Okay.

30
00:01:45,271 --> 00:01:46,314
Policy.

31
00:01:49,108 --> 00:01:52,028
Call. Make an appointment.
We'll talk as soon as possible.

32
00:01:52,153 --> 00:01:53,946
- I'm afraid I have to go.
- Yeah, no problem.

33
00:01:54,071 --> 00:01:56,240
I-I'm just gonna
wait outside, and, uh...

34
00:01:56,365 --> 00:01:57,408
- Mr. Jane...
- No, it's okay.

35
00:01:57,533 --> 00:01:58,993
It's a nice day. I'll take a walk.

36
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:01,078
And, um, if I come back
in three hours

37
00:02:01,287 --> 00:02:02,872
- will that be okay?
- Sure.

38
00:02:03,956 --> 00:02:04,999
Thank you.

39
00:02:05,124 --> 00:02:06,167
- Hey, Steve?
- Yeah.

40
00:02:06,375 --> 00:02:08,794
Would you help Mr. Jane
find his way out of the building?

41
00:02:12,423 --> 00:02:13,466
Sure.

42
00:02:33,027 --> 00:02:34,695
You--you work
on the Red John case?

43
00:02:35,863 --> 00:02:37,198
That's none of your business, sir.

44
00:02:39,283 --> 00:02:40,326
Have any suspects?

45
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:43,120
- Like I said.
- Ah. I...

46
00:02:49,835 --> 00:02:52,004
It's my--my wife and daughter.
I...

47
00:02:54,924 --> 00:02:56,801
Red John killed
my wife and daughter.

48
00:02:58,969 --> 00:03:00,429
Oh, well, uh...

49
00:03:01,305 --> 00:03:02,848
I'm very sorry for your loss.

50
00:03:03,432 --> 00:03:05,768
But we don't discuss cases
with the relatives of victims.

51
00:03:05,893 --> 00:03:07,395
Yeah, no. I-I understand.

52
00:03:10,314 --> 00:03:11,440
Listen, no offense

53
00:03:11,732 --> 00:03:13,609
but I seen a hundred guys
just like you.

54
00:03:14,985 --> 00:03:17,321
You wanna find this son of a bitch
and kill him, right?

55
00:03:18,948 --> 00:03:19,990
Yeah.

56
00:03:20,658 --> 00:03:21,992
Well, what happens

57
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:23,577
it'll drive you crazy.

58
00:03:24,036 --> 00:03:25,705
My advice? You move away.

59
00:03:26,163 --> 00:03:27,206
Far away somewhere.

60
00:03:27,331 --> 00:03:28,499
Forget it.
Start another family.

61
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:32,503
I know that's tough
but it's the best way.

62
00:03:34,630 --> 00:03:36,424
I just asked if
there were any suspects.

63
00:03:37,091 --> 00:03:39,176
One more time.
Let it go.

64
00:03:40,845 --> 00:03:41,887
Come on.

65
00:03:46,851 --> 00:03:48,144
What went wrong with you?

66
00:03:48,811 --> 00:03:49,854
Say what?

67
00:03:49,979 --> 00:03:52,440
Well, clearly, you're older and more
experienced than Agent Lisbon.

68
00:03:54,442 --> 00:03:55,943
You must have done something
pretty bad

69
00:03:56,068 --> 00:03:58,988
for them to promote a woman
20 years your junior over you.

70
00:03:59,447 --> 00:04:00,489
Who told you that?

71
00:04:01,323 --> 00:04:02,825
It's a temperament issue.

72
00:04:04,076 --> 00:04:05,327
As well as character.

73
00:04:06,078 --> 00:04:07,663
That's why they gave you
to Lisbon, isn't it?

74
00:04:07,788 --> 00:04:10,040
Because she was new, and no one
else would work with you.

75
00:04:14,795 --> 00:04:17,006
What the hell
are you doing, Hannigan?

76
00:04:17,256 --> 00:04:19,258
- Boss...
- I told you to take him downstairs

77
00:04:19,467 --> 00:04:20,509
not beat him up!

78
00:04:20,634 --> 00:04:22,261
Sorry, okay? I'm sorry.
I-I lost it.

79
00:04:22,428 --> 00:04:24,597
No, no. It--it's fine.
It's fine.

80
00:04:24,847 --> 00:04:26,432
My fault. My fault entirely.

81
00:04:26,557 --> 00:04:29,143
- I provoked you. I'm sorry.
- God, Hannigan, get him some ice.

82
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:34,231
I'm okay. I'm okay.

83
00:04:34,356 --> 00:04:38,360
Seriously, it--it's not his fault.
I-I deserved it, okay?

84
00:04:38,527 --> 00:04:40,863
He is supposed to act
like a professional law officer...

85
00:04:40,988 --> 00:04:42,031
at all times.

86
00:04:42,281 --> 00:04:44,158
Let's get you some ice.
Come on.

87
00:04:45,034 --> 00:04:46,076
Come on.

88
00:04:51,916 --> 00:04:53,417
Teresa Lisbon. That's a...

89
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:55,961
That's a nice name.

90
00:05:11,692 --> 00:05:12,734
How did it happen?

91
00:05:12,985 --> 00:05:15,195
Hannigan says he was provoked.
Mr. Jane agrees.

92
00:05:15,612 --> 00:05:16,822
He says it's all his fault.

93
00:05:17,573 --> 00:05:18,907
Decent of him.

94
00:05:21,201 --> 00:05:24,413
{\an8}A cop with a history attacks
a murder victim's grieving spouse.

95
00:05:25,247 --> 00:05:26,290
{\an8}Excellent.

96
00:05:27,249 --> 00:05:28,584
I'm sorry, boss.

97
00:05:29,835 --> 00:05:31,253
{\an8}I hope we can find a way
to make this right

98
00:05:31,378 --> 00:05:33,046
{\an8}without being too harsh
on Hannigan.

99
00:05:33,755 --> 00:05:35,674
{\an8}He's a good guy, he's just
a little too old school.

100
00:05:36,425 --> 00:05:38,176
{\an8}Mr. Jane says
he won't press charges.

101
00:05:38,844 --> 00:05:41,263
{\an8}Let's hope Mr. Jane
remains so amiable

102
00:05:41,555 --> 00:05:42,973
{\an8}when he wakes up
in the morning

103
00:05:43,181 --> 00:05:45,350
{\an8}with a pounding headache
and time to think.

104
00:05:47,811 --> 00:05:50,147
{\an8}We must find a way
to make him happy.

105
00:05:56,653 --> 00:05:57,696
Mr. Jane?

106
00:05:58,947 --> 00:06:00,824
Director Virgil Minelli.
No, no, no, no. Sit.

107
00:06:05,203 --> 00:06:08,498
{\an8}I'm, uh, I'm terribly sorry
about all of this.

108
00:06:08,916 --> 00:06:11,793
I understand that, um,
Agent Hannigan has apologized?

109
00:06:13,462 --> 00:06:15,380
Uh, yes, he did.
Mm-hmm.

110
00:06:15,505 --> 00:06:17,132
I hope that's been of some help.

111
00:06:18,008 --> 00:06:19,051
{\an8}Uh...

112
00:06:19,468 --> 00:06:20,719
{\an8}Um...

113
00:06:21,470 --> 00:06:25,891
{\an8}I-I came here to, uh,
find out about Red John.

114
00:06:26,808 --> 00:06:29,227
{\an8}Yes. Agent Lisbon told me.

115
00:06:29,645 --> 00:06:31,355
Uh, I understand your concern.

116
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:35,233
{\an8}Red John is one of the most
difficult cases we've faced.

117
00:06:37,402 --> 00:06:39,196
- How many victims, Lisbon?
- Ten.

118
00:06:40,364 --> 00:06:42,407
- So far.
- Yes.

119
00:06:42,824 --> 00:06:44,826
Catching him is our top priority.

120
00:06:45,535 --> 00:06:47,162
How many interviews
has your team done?

121
00:06:47,287 --> 00:06:48,330
{\an8}Over a hundred.

122
00:06:48,455 --> 00:06:50,457
{\an8}We're also re-analyzing
all of the physical evidence

123
00:06:50,582 --> 00:06:51,917
that Sac P.D. gathered.

124
00:06:52,167 --> 00:06:54,044
We're sharing some of that
with the FBI.

125
00:06:54,252 --> 00:06:56,630
{\an8}We're pursuing
a lot of different leads.

126
00:06:56,922 --> 00:06:57,965
{\an8}We haven't had a break yet

127
00:06:58,090 --> 00:06:59,800
{\an8}but as soon as we get one,
we'll let you know.

128
00:07:00,550 --> 00:07:01,593
What are the leads?

129
00:07:03,595 --> 00:07:04,638
Where are they leading?

130
00:07:07,432 --> 00:07:09,851
{\an8}You--you have any...
suspects?

131
00:07:10,268 --> 00:07:13,105
{\an8}We can't give out details
of the investigation.

132
00:07:13,647 --> 00:07:15,065
You don't have any suspects.

133
00:07:16,274 --> 00:07:19,778
{\an8}It is a complicated investigation,
and, yes, slow.

134
00:07:20,404 --> 00:07:22,239
But everything that can be done
is being done.

135
00:07:22,364 --> 00:07:23,573
I'll tell you what, Mr. Jane.

136
00:07:24,449 --> 00:07:26,535
My people have to get
back to work now.

137
00:07:26,743 --> 00:07:27,786
Long drive ahead of 'em.

138
00:07:27,953 --> 00:07:29,913
{\an8}But if you don't mind
waiting here

139
00:07:30,038 --> 00:07:31,790
{\an8}when, uh, Agent Lisbon returns

140
00:07:31,915 --> 00:07:33,709
{\an8}I'm sure she'll be very happy

141
00:07:33,917 --> 00:07:36,628
to show you the files
and explain the case to you.

142
00:07:38,755 --> 00:07:39,798
{\an8}Is it in the country?

143
00:07:40,924 --> 00:07:43,844
{\an8}The long drive ahead
is it--is it in the country?

144
00:07:45,637 --> 00:07:46,680
Would you like to go along?

145
00:07:49,641 --> 00:07:50,684
Even better.

146
00:07:51,518 --> 00:07:52,602
Ride along with Lisbon.

147
00:07:52,894 --> 00:07:56,231
She can answer any questions
you may have on the way.

148
00:07:56,690 --> 00:07:58,567
{\an8}- I'd like that.
- Good!

149
00:08:22,507 --> 00:08:23,550
Hey, boss.

150
00:08:24,926 --> 00:08:25,969
What's he doing here?

151
00:08:26,303 --> 00:08:27,846
Long story.

152
00:08:29,306 --> 00:08:31,391
- Patrick Jane. Hi.
- Cho.

153
00:08:33,268 --> 00:08:35,020
- Just pretend I'm not here.
- Okay.

154
00:08:35,562 --> 00:08:36,980
Victim's name is Winston Dellinger.

155
00:08:37,272 --> 00:08:39,191
Shot three times.
That's his car.

156
00:08:39,399 --> 00:08:41,318
Road crew came across his body
around 6:00 this morning.

157
00:08:41,526 --> 00:08:43,570
Coroner estimates
he was shot around midnight.

158
00:08:44,279 --> 00:08:45,864
There's some damage
on the front end.

159
00:08:45,989 --> 00:08:49,076
He must have hit something
so could be a road rage type thing?

160
00:08:49,201 --> 00:08:50,994
I doubt it.
There's no debris nearby.

161
00:08:51,995 --> 00:08:53,038
Widen the search.

162
00:08:53,163 --> 00:08:54,414
See if you can find out
where it did happen.

163
00:08:54,623 --> 00:08:56,083
- All right.
- This is Lisbon.

164
00:09:24,277 --> 00:09:25,320
What do you do now?

165
00:09:26,321 --> 00:09:28,156
Well, techs have done
their job

166
00:09:28,490 --> 00:09:29,699
took all the photos.

167
00:09:29,991 --> 00:09:31,034
We get up close.

168
00:09:37,707 --> 00:09:40,252
Well, you see, it looks like
he was shot right here.

169
00:09:41,253 --> 00:09:43,255
Note the natural posture
of the body.

170
00:09:43,421 --> 00:09:45,632
- And there's no drag marks.
- Uh-huh.

171
00:09:46,216 --> 00:09:47,259
Now this guy--

172
00:09:47,425 --> 00:09:49,761
this guy's pretty clean.
Pretty fresh.

173
00:09:50,428 --> 00:09:51,847
Sometimes we get to them

174
00:09:52,222 --> 00:09:55,058
there's so many maggots,
it looks like a stewpot boiling.

175
00:09:55,392 --> 00:09:59,146
Just poppin' and bubblin'.
And the smell--oh!

176
00:09:59,271 --> 00:10:01,273
Excuse me. Excuse me. Sorry.

177
00:10:03,859 --> 00:10:04,901
You all right?

178
00:10:05,527 --> 00:10:07,821
Yeah, I'm fine.
I just, uh...

179
00:10:08,488 --> 00:10:09,739
Oh, I'm just a little lightheaded.

180
00:10:11,449 --> 00:10:13,285
I told the coroner
they could take the body.

181
00:10:13,535 --> 00:10:16,163
We need to piece together
where Dellinger was before he got here.

182
00:10:16,288 --> 00:10:19,416
Work his cell phone, credit card bills.
Retrace his steps.

183
00:10:19,749 --> 00:10:21,668
- Okey-dokey.
- Find the lady.

184
00:10:23,503 --> 00:10:25,839
- What lady?
- The lady he was on a date with.

185
00:10:26,506 --> 00:10:29,426
Wow. So you are
some kinda psychic.

186
00:10:30,510 --> 00:10:31,928
How do you figure that, Kreskin?

187
00:10:32,596 --> 00:10:34,389
There's no such thing as psychics.

188
00:10:35,724 --> 00:10:37,559
He has a bachelor's car,
peacock clothes.

189
00:10:37,684 --> 00:10:39,477
He smells of alcohol
and breath mints

190
00:10:39,686 --> 00:10:40,854
and too much cologne.

191
00:10:42,898 --> 00:10:43,940
Date.

192
00:10:44,816 --> 00:10:46,526
Okay. Well, thank you
for your input.

193
00:10:47,527 --> 00:10:49,487
Cho, you got anything?

194
00:10:50,238 --> 00:10:52,365
Uniforms found a credit card
receipt in his car.

195
00:10:52,908 --> 00:10:54,242
He had dinner last night
at a restaurant

196
00:10:54,367 --> 00:10:55,535
called Cafe Tuscany.

197
00:10:56,369 --> 00:10:58,246
Go there. See what they can
tell you about him.

198
00:10:58,705 --> 00:11:00,874
The victim's father
was an appellate court judge.

199
00:11:01,124 --> 00:11:02,250
I need to go and talk to him.

200
00:11:02,626 --> 00:11:03,668
Roger that.

201
00:11:04,502 --> 00:11:05,629
I'm headed back to Sacramento.

202
00:11:05,754 --> 00:11:07,297
You want me to drop you off
somewhere on the way?

203
00:11:07,672 --> 00:11:08,715
I'll go with you.

204
00:11:30,445 --> 00:11:32,656
Uh, so how does this work?

205
00:11:32,864 --> 00:11:35,533
I go in. Ask the people questions.

206
00:11:35,742 --> 00:11:38,536
They're probably pretty upset.
May not be able to tell me much.

207
00:11:40,121 --> 00:11:43,458
It doesn't help to have
other people around.

208
00:11:44,501 --> 00:11:46,795
- You--you want me to stay here?
- I would prefer that.

209
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:49,547
Sure. No--no problem.
I don't--I don't want to intrude.

210
00:11:51,299 --> 00:11:53,885
Agent Lisbon, do you mind
if we talk out here?

211
00:11:54,135 --> 00:11:56,096
My wife's extremely distraught.

212
00:11:56,304 --> 00:11:58,306
I'd rather she didn't hear us.

213
00:11:59,599 --> 00:12:01,393
This is, um, Patrick Jane.

214
00:12:02,143 --> 00:12:03,645
Pleasure. This way, please.

215
00:12:10,735 --> 00:12:13,154
Had you and your wife heard
from your son recently?

216
00:12:13,780 --> 00:12:15,407
We spoke on the phone
last week.

217
00:12:16,283 --> 00:12:17,742
Was he in some sorta trouble?

218
00:12:18,118 --> 00:12:21,121
Agent, I have the sickening feeling

219
00:12:21,329 --> 00:12:23,373
that this had nothing
to do with Winston.

220
00:12:23,707 --> 00:12:25,083
What do you mean by that?

221
00:12:25,292 --> 00:12:28,211
I've put a lot of desperate individuals
into prison over the years.

222
00:12:28,336 --> 00:12:30,463
Any one of them
might be behind this.

223
00:12:30,714 --> 00:12:32,799
Why would they go after him?
Why not you?

224
00:12:33,508 --> 00:12:34,718
You wanna hurt a man?

225
00:12:35,969 --> 00:12:37,012
Don't kill him.

226
00:12:38,138 --> 00:12:39,431
Kill his family.

227
00:12:42,892 --> 00:12:44,436
We'll certainly look into that.

228
00:12:45,687 --> 00:12:46,730
Alcoholism.

229
00:12:48,148 --> 00:12:49,524
Terrible thing.

230
00:12:50,108 --> 00:12:52,027
Winston was drinking again?

231
00:12:52,193 --> 00:12:55,322
We won't know until after
we get the lab reports back.

232
00:12:55,697 --> 00:12:56,740
So...

233
00:12:58,533 --> 00:13:01,119
You're simply casting aspersions?

234
00:13:01,453 --> 00:13:02,912
No. I--I just...

235
00:13:03,788 --> 00:13:05,874
I assumed from your manner...

236
00:13:06,499 --> 00:13:07,584
From what manner, sir?

237
00:13:08,835 --> 00:13:10,503
Your disappointment in him.

238
00:13:11,212 --> 00:13:13,048
With regard to my son, Mr. Jane

239
00:13:14,049 --> 00:13:15,675
it's myself I'm disappointed in.

240
00:13:17,969 --> 00:13:20,847
He's my failure.
Do you have a child, Mr. Jane?

241
00:13:22,015 --> 00:13:23,058
No.

242
00:13:24,476 --> 00:13:25,727
Well, then you wouldn't understand.

243
00:13:27,604 --> 00:13:29,105
If there's nothing else,
Agent Lisbon...

244
00:13:30,982 --> 00:13:32,025
No, sir.

245
00:13:36,446 --> 00:13:38,990
"Dellinger chairs
the Fifth Circuit Appeals Court."

246
00:13:39,366 --> 00:13:42,619
Do you know how much trouble
I could get in if he's pissed off?

247
00:13:42,869 --> 00:13:44,871
- No. How much?
- A lot.

248
00:13:45,246 --> 00:13:46,289
What you have to understand--

249
00:13:48,249 --> 00:13:49,292
Yeah?

250
00:13:50,502 --> 00:13:51,544
Hang on, Cho.

251
00:13:56,966 --> 00:13:58,009
Excuse me.

252
00:14:05,308 --> 00:14:06,351
Go on.

253
00:14:06,935 --> 00:14:08,895
Just talked to the maître d'
at Cafe Tuscany.

254
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:10,897
Said Dellinger came in
last night with a woman.

255
00:14:11,064 --> 00:14:12,482
"Said she seemed
a little low-rent."

256
00:14:12,816 --> 00:14:15,068
"Dellinger got so drunk
the woman left before dinner arrived."

257
00:14:15,235 --> 00:14:16,277
Really?

258
00:14:16,444 --> 00:14:18,530
"Also talked to the cab company
that picked up Dellinger's date."

259
00:14:19,030 --> 00:14:20,949
Her name's Kelly Burbage.
She's coming in tomorrow.

260
00:14:21,282 --> 00:14:22,325
Thanks.

261
00:14:26,329 --> 00:14:27,372
You were right.

262
00:14:27,705 --> 00:14:30,291
The victim was on a date.
Good call.

263
00:14:31,376 --> 00:14:33,628
- Cold reading.
- Cold reading?

264
00:14:35,088 --> 00:14:36,714
You, for instance. You...

265
00:14:37,465 --> 00:14:38,967
cared for a dysfunctional parent.

266
00:14:39,300 --> 00:14:41,594
Father, probably. That's why
you put up with Hannigan.

267
00:14:42,095 --> 00:14:43,596
I don't put up with Hannigan.

268
00:14:44,472 --> 00:14:47,517
His unhappiness reminds you
of your father's unhappiness.

269
00:14:49,310 --> 00:14:50,437
We're done for the day.

270
00:14:50,895 --> 00:14:52,439
Is there somewhere
I could drop you off?

271
00:14:54,190 --> 00:14:56,109
What about the Red John files?

272
00:14:57,902 --> 00:15:01,197
Mr. Jane, I truly sympathize.

273
00:15:01,656 --> 00:15:03,158
I understand how you're feeling.

274
00:15:03,324 --> 00:15:05,410
I would probably feel the same way.

275
00:15:06,327 --> 00:15:08,788
But nothing good will come
from chasing this man.

276
00:15:09,831 --> 00:15:11,916
It's the kind of obsession
that destroys people.

277
00:15:13,668 --> 00:15:14,711
Go someplace else.

278
00:15:17,672 --> 00:15:18,882
Try to get on with your life.

279
00:15:21,259 --> 00:15:22,886
That's just what Hannigan said.

280
00:15:30,393 --> 00:15:33,229
Come to the office in the morning.
But clean yourself up.

281
00:15:34,856 --> 00:15:35,899
You're a mess.

282
00:15:43,865 --> 00:15:44,908
Get in.

283
00:16:01,956 --> 00:16:02,999
Hi.

284
00:16:04,459 --> 00:16:05,501
Hey.

285
00:16:05,626 --> 00:16:07,003
It's Kimball Cho, isn't it?

286
00:16:07,161 --> 00:16:09,330
Is that after the Kipling character?

287
00:16:09,664 --> 00:16:10,915
No. Why are you still here?

288
00:16:11,249 --> 00:16:13,126
Agent Lisbon told me to come by.

289
00:16:13,584 --> 00:16:15,503
To read the Red John files.

290
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:16,963
- Hey.
- Hey.

291
00:16:21,134 --> 00:16:23,302
Lisbon told him to come by.
Read the Red John files.

292
00:16:24,512 --> 00:16:25,555
Hi.

293
00:16:26,013 --> 00:16:27,348
All right. Hi.

294
00:16:28,307 --> 00:16:29,851
Oh, pretend I'm not here.

295
00:16:30,810 --> 00:16:32,186
Uh, okay.

296
00:16:32,311 --> 00:16:33,688
Kelly Burbage. Girl who had dinner
with the victim.

297
00:16:33,855 --> 00:16:35,857
- Interview three.
- All right. Thanks.

298
00:16:45,366 --> 00:16:46,659
You can take the desk
over there.

299
00:16:47,326 --> 00:16:48,369
No one's using that.

300
00:16:53,749 --> 00:16:54,792
Uh, yeah.

301
00:16:58,546 --> 00:16:59,589
Miss Burbage...

302
00:17:01,007 --> 00:17:02,425
how do you know
Winston Dellinger?

303
00:17:03,551 --> 00:17:06,679
I work tending bar
at the Thirsty Pup in Hagginwood?

304
00:17:07,513 --> 00:17:09,849
- Winston's a regular.
- He has a drinking problem.

305
00:17:10,975 --> 00:17:13,019
- It's a bar.
- What happened at dinner?

306
00:17:13,394 --> 00:17:14,645
What I shoulda known.

307
00:17:14,896 --> 00:17:16,731
He climbed through
two bottles of house red

308
00:17:16,981 --> 00:17:18,983
before I even got
my pasta pomodoro.

309
00:17:20,151 --> 00:17:21,777
I told him he was too drunk
to drive me home.

310
00:17:22,028 --> 00:17:23,529
He got mad, I got a cab.

311
00:17:25,323 --> 00:17:28,159
Look, if this is because Winston did
something last night

312
00:17:28,409 --> 00:17:29,994
it's just because
he was smashed.

313
00:17:30,495 --> 00:17:33,623
- He wouldn't hurt a fly.
- He's dead. He was killed last night.

314
00:17:33,748 --> 00:17:34,790
What?

315
00:17:34,957 --> 00:17:36,000
Somebody shot him.

316
00:17:36,417 --> 00:17:38,336
About two hours
after he left the restaurant.

317
00:17:38,669 --> 00:17:40,046
Any idea
who might have done that?

318
00:17:44,091 --> 00:17:46,302
- Oh, my God.
- That sounds like "yes".

319
00:17:47,803 --> 00:17:49,639
There's--there's this guy...

320
00:17:50,264 --> 00:17:51,307
we used to date

321
00:17:51,724 --> 00:17:55,353
but I broke it off because he was
this gigantic ball of negativity.

322
00:17:55,520 --> 00:17:56,562
Sure.

323
00:17:56,687 --> 00:17:58,606
He called me last night
after I got home.

324
00:17:58,898 --> 00:17:59,941
Totally messed up.

325
00:18:00,441 --> 00:18:02,527
He said he'd followed me
on the date.

326
00:18:03,819 --> 00:18:06,072
He kept talking
about what a loser Winston was

327
00:18:06,197 --> 00:18:08,241
- and how he didn't deserve me.
- What's his name?

328
00:18:08,991 --> 00:18:10,034
Emmett.

329
00:18:10,868 --> 00:18:12,036
Emmett Cox.

330
00:18:13,955 --> 00:18:14,997
Hey, boss.

331
00:18:16,165 --> 00:18:18,501
Cox has two arrests for assault
and a gun charge pending.

332
00:18:18,626 --> 00:18:19,669
Nice.

333
00:18:20,002 --> 00:18:22,255
- Is this address still current?
- Burbage thinks so.

334
00:18:22,547 --> 00:18:24,882
You and Hannigan see if you can
locate him, bring him in.

335
00:18:25,091 --> 00:18:27,426
Seems like a real charmer.
Full S.W.A.T. protocol.

336
00:18:31,514 --> 00:18:32,848
He said you said
he was allowed to be here.

337
00:18:33,057 --> 00:18:36,018
Yes, I did.
I didn't think he'd actually show up.

338
00:18:37,144 --> 00:18:38,479
- Go get Cox.
- Yes, boss.

339
00:18:39,480 --> 00:18:40,523
Mr. Jane!

340
00:18:46,612 --> 00:18:47,655
Mr. Jane.

341
00:18:48,447 --> 00:18:51,242
- You--you can call me Patrick.
- Patrick, have a seat.

342
00:18:59,041 --> 00:19:00,293
You were hoping
I wouldn't come back?

343
00:19:01,544 --> 00:19:02,587
Yes.

344
00:19:03,129 --> 00:19:05,339
Frankly, I don't think
you should look at the files.

345
00:19:06,048 --> 00:19:07,300
Your boss said I could.

346
00:19:10,052 --> 00:19:11,095
You're right.

347
00:19:12,096 --> 00:19:14,223
I should probably just start a new life.

348
00:19:17,435 --> 00:19:18,477
I can't.

349
00:19:21,480 --> 00:19:23,774
I will have the files sent up.
There's a lot of them.

350
00:19:24,275 --> 00:19:25,401
Meanwhile, you stay in here.

351
00:19:25,610 --> 00:19:27,903
I don't mind waiting out there.
I don't wanna be a burden.

352
00:19:28,779 --> 00:19:30,990
You're kind of a distraction
to the office.

353
00:19:31,616 --> 00:19:34,285
No offense, but you have a bit
of a homeless vibe about you.

354
00:19:34,660 --> 00:19:37,079
I cleaned up,
like you, uh, told me to.

355
00:19:37,997 --> 00:19:39,248
It's a process, huh?

356
00:19:43,085 --> 00:19:44,128
Hm. Well.

357
00:19:48,299 --> 00:19:49,717
- Get in here.
- Come on, Cox.

358
00:19:51,636 --> 00:19:53,638
Have a seat. Go on.
Scoot up.

359
00:19:55,681 --> 00:19:57,683
"There you go. That's it."

360
00:20:00,353 --> 00:20:02,563
Okay, Emmett, cut the crap
and tell us what happened.

361
00:20:02,813 --> 00:20:03,981
Bite me.
I done nothing wrong.

362
00:20:06,901 --> 00:20:08,194
Well, if you done nothing wrong

363
00:20:08,986 --> 00:20:10,988
then there's no reason
not to tell us what happened.

364
00:20:11,947 --> 00:20:12,990
Give us something.

365
00:20:15,451 --> 00:20:17,078
I followed Kel and that dude
to the restaurant.

366
00:20:17,953 --> 00:20:19,538
Kel came out
and got in a cab.

367
00:20:19,789 --> 00:20:21,248
A few minutes later,
that dude came out.

368
00:20:21,457 --> 00:20:23,417
By "that dude" you mean
Winston Dellinger?

369
00:20:24,251 --> 00:20:25,294
If that's his name.

370
00:20:25,503 --> 00:20:27,254
He got in his car,
so I followed him.

371
00:20:27,421 --> 00:20:28,464
Now why'd you do that?

372
00:20:32,468 --> 00:20:34,553
Honesty, I was thinking
I'd follow him home.

373
00:20:34,762 --> 00:20:36,722
Mess him up a little.
Take his money and whatnot.

374
00:20:37,348 --> 00:20:38,891
But no harm, no foul, right?

375
00:20:40,309 --> 00:20:41,352
Well...

376
00:20:42,520 --> 00:20:44,730
Winston Dellinger's dead.

377
00:20:45,231 --> 00:20:46,273
That's not on me.

378
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:48,317
The dude was driving too fast
and I couldn't keep up

379
00:20:48,567 --> 00:20:49,610
so I went home.

380
00:20:53,781 --> 00:20:55,783
Well, you know what I think?

381
00:20:56,617 --> 00:20:59,370
I think when the dude
pulled over to relieve himself

382
00:20:59,704 --> 00:21:01,205
you drove up behind him

383
00:21:01,580 --> 00:21:03,791
and you thought, "Hey, cool."

384
00:21:03,958 --> 00:21:05,126
"Why not jack him right here?"

385
00:21:05,251 --> 00:21:07,169
"Save time, save trouble".

386
00:21:08,379 --> 00:21:09,422
That's what I think.

387
00:21:09,797 --> 00:21:10,840
"You can think what you like."

388
00:21:15,886 --> 00:21:18,305
All I'm saying is if you will
let me go at him again

389
00:21:18,472 --> 00:21:20,015
Cox will open up.

390
00:21:20,182 --> 00:21:22,101
I don't know.
I think he's telling the truth.

391
00:21:22,893 --> 00:21:23,936
Where are we?

392
00:21:24,061 --> 00:21:26,647
I went through the threats
made against Judge Dellinger.

393
00:21:26,772 --> 00:21:28,357
Doesn't look like any of these guys
have the kinda pull

394
00:21:28,482 --> 00:21:30,067
to reach outta prison
and kill Winston.

395
00:21:33,946 --> 00:21:34,989
What are you doing?

396
00:21:35,656 --> 00:21:37,408
Uh, just stretching my legs.

397
00:21:41,245 --> 00:21:42,288
Anything else?

398
00:21:42,747 --> 00:21:44,498
Yeah. Ballistics came back.

399
00:21:45,958 --> 00:21:48,043
Bullets in the body
match the bullets from a gun

400
00:21:48,169 --> 00:21:50,212
used in an armed robbery
in Oakland 12 years ago.

401
00:21:50,546 --> 00:21:52,506
Those guys are in prison.
The gun was never recovered.

402
00:21:52,631 --> 00:21:54,842
- Someone else must have gotten it.
- I got something.

403
00:21:55,134 --> 00:21:57,720
Nine months ago, Winston was
charged with vehicular manslaughter.

404
00:21:57,845 --> 00:21:59,889
D.A. said he hit and killed a woman
named Mia Dos Santos

405
00:22:00,014 --> 00:22:01,682
- while driving drunk.
- Well, what happened?

406
00:22:01,849 --> 00:22:04,018
The manslaughter charge was dropped
before it went to trial.

407
00:22:04,268 --> 00:22:06,187
He pleaded to a D.U.I.,
no jail time.

408
00:22:06,479 --> 00:22:08,022
- Well, how does that happen?
- You got me.

409
00:22:08,147 --> 00:22:10,191
Dos Santos' husband was mad
when the charge got dropped.

410
00:22:10,441 --> 00:22:12,276
- He made some threats.
- Who handled the case?

411
00:22:12,401 --> 00:22:14,195
Sac P.D. detective
named Nathaniel Kim.

412
00:22:14,528 --> 00:22:16,697
- Talk to him. I'll talk to the husband.
- Okay.

413
00:22:17,072 --> 00:22:18,199
Where are the Red John files?

414
00:22:18,324 --> 00:22:19,366
They were supposed
to be here by now.

415
00:22:19,533 --> 00:22:20,576
Yeah, they're on their way.

416
00:22:20,701 --> 00:22:22,411
The office remodel's got
the records department backed up.

417
00:22:22,620 --> 00:22:25,122
Great. Wonderful.
Tell them to get their butts in gear.

418
00:22:25,956 --> 00:22:27,708
Hey. You.
You're coming with me.

419
00:22:29,877 --> 00:22:31,587
"I'm looking
for Detective Nathaniel Kim."

420
00:22:31,879 --> 00:22:32,922
"You got him."

421
00:22:33,130 --> 00:22:34,548
I work here on my off days.

422
00:22:35,299 --> 00:22:36,634
You know, Sac P.D.'s great

423
00:22:36,759 --> 00:22:39,136
but alimony and child support
are a bitch.

424
00:22:42,014 --> 00:22:43,974
- This about Winston Dellinger?
- That's right.

425
00:22:45,768 --> 00:22:49,230
Yeah, well. Dellinger knocked poor
Mia Dos Santos right out of her shoes.

426
00:22:49,647 --> 00:22:50,731
She had three kids.

427
00:22:51,857 --> 00:22:52,900
That's tough.

428
00:22:53,192 --> 00:22:54,902
And why did the manslaughter charge
get dropped?

429
00:22:55,152 --> 00:22:57,988
We only had circumstantial evidence
putting Winston at the scene.

430
00:22:58,405 --> 00:23:00,407
Nobody actually saw him hit her.

431
00:23:00,908 --> 00:23:02,743
But we did have blood on his car.

432
00:23:03,327 --> 00:23:04,453
Seemed like a dunk.

433
00:23:04,954 --> 00:23:06,580
Lab results come back

434
00:23:06,872 --> 00:23:08,624
blood doesn't belong
to Mia Dos Santos.

435
00:23:09,041 --> 00:23:10,584
No dunk. No case.

436
00:23:11,126 --> 00:23:12,670
We were lucky to get the D.U.I.

437
00:23:12,962 --> 00:23:14,338
Did you double-check
the lab results?

438
00:23:14,505 --> 00:23:16,340
Sure. Came back the same.

439
00:23:16,507 --> 00:23:17,883
And Winston's father's a judge.

440
00:23:18,300 --> 00:23:19,718
He knows people
all through the system.

441
00:23:20,094 --> 00:23:21,846
Yes, he is, and, yes, he does.

442
00:23:21,971 --> 00:23:24,139
You ever consider
the possibility he reached out

443
00:23:24,306 --> 00:23:25,975
made sure his son
didn't go to prison?

444
00:23:26,267 --> 00:23:28,978
Sure, I thought it.
Wouldn't say it.

445
00:23:29,103 --> 00:23:30,145
Why not?

446
00:23:30,271 --> 00:23:31,897
Guy's a freakin'' Tyrannosaurus rex.

447
00:23:32,231 --> 00:23:34,942
I'm gonna accuse him of obstruction
of justice on a hunch?

448
00:23:35,901 --> 00:23:36,944
You do it.

449
00:23:37,736 --> 00:23:38,779
What can I get you?

450
00:23:44,410 --> 00:23:47,496
Have you heard anything
about Winston Dellinger recently?

451
00:23:48,122 --> 00:23:49,456
I heard he was killed.

452
00:23:49,748 --> 00:23:50,791
Is that right?

453
00:23:50,916 --> 00:23:53,002
Where did you hear that,
Mr. Dos Santos?

454
00:23:53,961 --> 00:23:55,004
Not sure.

455
00:23:55,880 --> 00:23:57,631
Our lawyers, I think.

456
00:23:58,007 --> 00:24:01,135
You know, we were preparing
a, uh, wrongful death lawsuit

457
00:24:01,427 --> 00:24:02,469
against Dellinger.

458
00:24:03,888 --> 00:24:05,014
It's not gonna happen now.

459
00:24:05,514 --> 00:24:07,600
And have you been in contact
with Mr. Dellinger

460
00:24:07,725 --> 00:24:08,934
since your wife's death?

461
00:24:09,101 --> 00:24:11,353
No. Not recently.

462
00:24:11,854 --> 00:24:13,606
After the charges were dropped

463
00:24:13,731 --> 00:24:16,817
didn't you seek him out,
threaten him several times?

464
00:24:18,152 --> 00:24:19,194
Yeah.

465
00:24:20,487 --> 00:24:21,655
I was really angry.

466
00:24:23,073 --> 00:24:25,367
And I said some angry things.

467
00:24:27,036 --> 00:24:29,371
I shouldn't have done that.
Stupid.

468
00:24:30,497 --> 00:24:32,207
No. No, it wasn't.

469
00:24:33,542 --> 00:24:35,210
That man killed my daughter.

470
00:24:35,794 --> 00:24:37,838
And he left her babies
without their mother.

471
00:24:38,005 --> 00:24:39,423
And nothing happens to him?

472
00:24:40,215 --> 00:24:42,509
You should've done more.
You should've hurt him!

473
00:24:42,635 --> 00:24:44,720
You should've hurt him
the way that he hurt us!

474
00:25:07,034 --> 00:25:08,077
What have we got?

475
00:25:08,369 --> 00:25:10,079
Ran Christian Dos Santos.

476
00:25:10,371 --> 00:25:13,040
No arrests, but he's had trouble
at work since his wife died.

477
00:25:13,999 --> 00:25:16,710
Issues with customers. He's taking
an anger management course.

478
00:25:16,919 --> 00:25:18,837
- And what about the judge?
- We checked his bank accounts.

479
00:25:18,963 --> 00:25:21,674
No significant money transfers
when the murder charge was withdrawn.

480
00:25:22,007 --> 00:25:23,842
If he paid someone off,
there's no sign of it.

481
00:25:24,093 --> 00:25:25,886
Still no sign of where
Winston Dellinger's car

482
00:25:26,095 --> 00:25:27,221
had an accident
the night he was killed.

483
00:25:27,346 --> 00:25:29,098
There's some uniforms out there
looking for debris.

484
00:25:31,517 --> 00:25:32,559
That's it?

485
00:25:32,935 --> 00:25:34,603
Well, it's a hard case, boss.

486
00:25:35,312 --> 00:25:36,355
Let's start from the top.

487
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:38,023
Bring in everybody
involved in the case.

488
00:25:38,148 --> 00:25:39,483
We'll hear their stories again.

489
00:25:39,692 --> 00:25:42,027
- Maybe something will shake loose.
- Will do.

490
00:25:42,361 --> 00:25:43,862
First batch of Red John.

491
00:25:44,530 --> 00:25:45,572
Where do you want 'em?

492
00:25:46,281 --> 00:25:47,700
Uh, you can just leave it there.

493
00:25:54,373 --> 00:25:55,416
Eager beaver, huh?

494
00:26:07,636 --> 00:26:08,679
Mr. Jane

495
00:26:09,013 --> 00:26:11,724
before you get into that
I wanted to ask a favor.

496
00:26:14,101 --> 00:26:15,144
I need your help.

497
00:26:24,584 --> 00:26:28,254
Okay. Everybody involved in
the Dellinger murder is in that room.

498
00:26:28,713 --> 00:26:30,840
One of them is very likely lying.

499
00:26:31,091 --> 00:26:32,926
One of them is very likely
the murderer.

500
00:26:33,301 --> 00:26:34,344
Wow.

501
00:26:34,677 --> 00:26:36,596
What I'd like you to do
is go in there

502
00:26:36,888 --> 00:26:39,891
take a look at all of them
and tell me if you can spot the liar.

503
00:26:40,809 --> 00:26:43,061
- Me?
- You seem to have a gift.

504
00:26:44,020 --> 00:26:45,897
I told you, I'm not a psychic.

505
00:26:46,022 --> 00:26:47,774
I'm a charlatan.
You hear me?

506
00:26:47,899 --> 00:26:49,401
I-I-I'm a fraud.

507
00:26:49,567 --> 00:26:52,737
I believe you.
But whatever it is, it's a gift.

508
00:26:52,946 --> 00:26:54,322
I figure, why not use it?

509
00:26:59,536 --> 00:27:01,788
- I can't.
- We're kind of at a standstill here.

510
00:27:03,415 --> 00:27:04,457
Come on.

511
00:27:10,171 --> 00:27:12,048
Hello, everybody.

512
00:27:12,882 --> 00:27:15,718
Um, this is Patrick Jane.
He's a consultant with the CBI.

513
00:27:16,177 --> 00:27:17,595
Before we start the interviews

514
00:27:17,929 --> 00:27:20,348
he's gonna... we'll see
what he's gonna do.

515
00:27:20,765 --> 00:27:21,808
Mr. Jane?

516
00:27:31,693 --> 00:27:32,735
Hi, folks.

517
00:27:33,319 --> 00:27:35,697
Quick question--which one of you
killed Winston Dellinger?

518
00:27:35,822 --> 00:27:37,490
- Oh, come on. This is ridiculous.
- What?

519
00:27:37,657 --> 00:27:39,451
- I'm not gonna sit here and listen to this.
- Is he serious?

520
00:27:39,701 --> 00:27:42,454
Everybody just calm down, please.

521
00:27:43,329 --> 00:27:44,372
That was worth a try.

522
00:27:44,497 --> 00:27:47,459
Uh, Agents Cho and Rigsby
will proceed with the interviews.

523
00:27:47,667 --> 00:27:48,710
Thank you very much.

524
00:27:49,127 --> 00:27:51,296
- Judge, if you'll come with me.
- Uh, wait a minute.

525
00:27:51,421 --> 00:27:52,630
- I think I know who did it.
- You sure?

526
00:27:52,964 --> 00:27:54,007
Pretty sure.

527
00:27:54,591 --> 00:27:56,968
If everybody could just
please sit back down.

528
00:27:57,302 --> 00:28:00,138
My apologies. Please.

529
00:28:01,598 --> 00:28:02,640
Now what?

530
00:28:05,226 --> 00:28:07,687
- You are absolutely sure?
- Uh, 70%.

531
00:28:10,273 --> 00:28:11,399
You have tarot cards?

532
00:28:13,276 --> 00:28:14,861
- Tarot cards?
- No.

533
00:28:15,153 --> 00:28:18,573
Uh, ladies and gentlemen,
um, I-I'm sorry

534
00:28:18,698 --> 00:28:21,784
for, uh, for wasting your time.

535
00:28:21,910 --> 00:28:24,537
- If, uh...
- I've had more than enough of this.

536
00:28:24,787 --> 00:28:28,416
Agent Lisbon, really?
This is outrageous.

537
00:28:28,583 --> 00:28:30,668
- Tell him, Judge.
- Just one moment more.

538
00:28:30,877 --> 00:28:31,920
There's something
I wanna show you.

539
00:28:32,045 --> 00:28:34,339
Something you might
find amazing.

540
00:28:36,216 --> 00:28:37,467
I used to be a psychic.

541
00:28:38,301 --> 00:28:41,054
I used to read minds, talk to dead people.
Only I didn't.

542
00:28:41,888 --> 00:28:43,556
Of course I didn't,
'cause there's no such thing

543
00:28:43,681 --> 00:28:46,976
as psychics or mediums,
or at least I've never met one.

544
00:28:47,936 --> 00:28:50,063
Psychic powers are just tricks.
They're mind games.

545
00:28:50,230 --> 00:28:52,065
It's observation.
But it works.

546
00:28:54,150 --> 00:28:55,902
There's a killer in this room

547
00:28:56,528 --> 00:28:58,988
and I'm gonna use
pseudo-psychic powers

548
00:28:59,113 --> 00:29:01,574
to persuade that killer
to confess.

549
00:29:02,408 --> 00:29:03,451
This is bull.

550
00:29:04,744 --> 00:29:07,121
Shortcut method--the first person
to leave did it.

551
00:29:16,089 --> 00:29:18,383
Now like I say, there's
no such thing as psychics.

552
00:29:20,134 --> 00:29:21,261
Let's be clear about that.

553
00:29:23,429 --> 00:29:27,559
But the human mind
is amazingly powerful.

554
00:29:29,519 --> 00:29:33,690
It can do things for real
that sometimes feel like magic.

555
00:29:34,649 --> 00:29:35,692
And I wanna show you.

556
00:29:36,067 --> 00:29:40,530
Now, normally, I would use
Tarot cards for this.

557
00:29:41,155 --> 00:29:44,242
But, uh, in this case,
these will have to do

558
00:29:44,742 --> 00:29:47,412
as long as you're all willing
to use a little imagination.

559
00:29:50,206 --> 00:29:51,249
Bear with me.

560
00:29:55,587 --> 00:29:57,589
Agent Lisbon, if you could, uh...

561
00:29:57,714 --> 00:29:59,882
mix those cards up
thoroughly, please.

562
00:30:00,383 --> 00:30:01,759
Thank you for your patience.

563
00:30:05,930 --> 00:30:07,473
- There you go.
- Thank you.

564
00:30:09,017 --> 00:30:10,059
Now...

565
00:30:13,563 --> 00:30:16,441
I would like you, without looking

566
00:30:17,442 --> 00:30:20,320
to choose a card,
face-down, but first--

567
00:30:20,778 --> 00:30:22,238
and this is very important--

568
00:30:22,447 --> 00:30:24,490
before you take the card
I'd like you to close your eyes

569
00:30:24,699 --> 00:30:27,118
and I'd like you to think
about the last scary dream you had.

570
00:30:29,203 --> 00:30:30,747
Remember the last time
you woke up

571
00:30:30,872 --> 00:30:32,582
shivering with fear.

572
00:30:38,296 --> 00:30:41,716
Got it? Good.
Thank you. Open your eyes.

573
00:30:44,427 --> 00:30:47,180
Take a card.
Keep it face-down.

574
00:30:48,931 --> 00:30:50,516
Keep your hand on top of it.

575
00:31:02,403 --> 00:31:03,446
Thank you.

576
00:31:03,905 --> 00:31:05,156
Now here's the thing--

577
00:31:06,616 --> 00:31:08,368
you think you just made
a random pick.

578
00:31:08,576 --> 00:31:11,120
Where, in fact, your subconscious mind

579
00:31:11,496 --> 00:31:13,122
made a very meaningful choice.

580
00:31:14,207 --> 00:31:15,917
And this is how the killer
will be revealed.

581
00:31:19,837 --> 00:31:21,172
Mrs. Recinos

582
00:31:21,339 --> 00:31:24,175
you dreamt that your daughter
was falling into a very dark place

583
00:31:24,467 --> 00:31:26,094
and you couldn't stop her.

584
00:31:26,844 --> 00:31:29,764
You called out that you loved her
but she couldn't hear you.

585
00:31:30,723 --> 00:31:33,184
- Yes.
- And that's why you chose the lovers.

586
00:31:44,028 --> 00:31:45,988
Judge Dellinger,
you dreamt of death.

587
00:31:47,990 --> 00:31:49,283
And you chose death.

588
00:31:55,748 --> 00:31:59,669
Kelly, you can't shake the idea
that you'll never find true love.

589
00:32:00,795 --> 00:32:02,463
And you picked the fool.

590
00:32:07,009 --> 00:32:08,052
How do you do that?

591
00:32:09,679 --> 00:32:10,722
Mr. Kim.

592
00:32:11,931 --> 00:32:13,683
You have a lot of scary dreams.

593
00:32:15,560 --> 00:32:16,602
But you can't remember them.

594
00:32:17,979 --> 00:32:20,648
However, you're a cop.

595
00:32:21,524 --> 00:32:24,110
So you think the rules
don't apply to you.

596
00:32:26,738 --> 00:32:29,073
And you chose the magician.

597
00:32:34,954 --> 00:32:36,831
- Neat trick.
- Yes, just a trick.

598
00:32:36,956 --> 00:32:39,667
Mr. Dos Santos, you dream
of being trapped.

599
00:32:39,917 --> 00:32:41,794
Caged like an animal.

600
00:32:42,462 --> 00:32:45,798
And you dream of a terrible,
violent escape.

601
00:32:47,049 --> 00:32:48,509
You picked the devil.

602
00:32:52,430 --> 00:32:53,639
None of that's true.

603
00:32:54,724 --> 00:32:56,851
And, Mr. Cox.

604
00:32:57,351 --> 00:32:59,604
You constantly dream
of all the people you've hurt

605
00:32:59,937 --> 00:33:01,898
coming back to seek revenge.

606
00:33:02,940 --> 00:33:05,818
And guess what?
They have the same dream.

607
00:33:07,028 --> 00:33:09,614
You chose the hanged man.

608
00:33:15,411 --> 00:33:18,372
Uh, actually that's not... right.

609
00:33:20,124 --> 00:33:22,710
Uh, Mr. Kim had that card.

610
00:33:27,298 --> 00:33:28,341
Ah.

611
00:33:33,179 --> 00:33:34,222
Uh-huh.

612
00:33:38,518 --> 00:33:39,852
What's that supposed to mean?

613
00:33:41,562 --> 00:33:43,439
It means you killed
Winston Dellinger.

614
00:33:47,401 --> 00:33:50,321
- Yeah, right. Give me a break.
- No. No break. You did it.

615
00:33:50,988 --> 00:33:52,615
The subconscious mind
never lies.

616
00:33:52,740 --> 00:33:54,659
Your guilt is written
on that card...

617
00:33:55,576 --> 00:33:57,787
- and written all over your face.
- No.

618
00:33:57,912 --> 00:33:59,997
No, I-I didn't. Come on.
It's a card trick.

619
00:34:00,122 --> 00:34:03,167
Yes, it was, but when I said
I could use your choice of card

620
00:34:03,292 --> 00:34:06,462
to reveal the killer,
you looked a little worried.

621
00:34:07,755 --> 00:34:09,966
For a split second.
Just you.

622
00:34:10,091 --> 00:34:12,844
And then you looked relieved
when I couldn't read your dream.

623
00:34:12,969 --> 00:34:14,345
And then when you saw
the hanged man

624
00:34:14,470 --> 00:34:16,764
- the blood drained from your face.
- No.

625
00:34:17,473 --> 00:34:20,059
- No, this is ridiculous.
- Everyone can see your guilt.

626
00:34:20,184 --> 00:34:22,144
But what I can't see
is your motive.

627
00:34:23,312 --> 00:34:24,689
Why, Nathaniel?

628
00:34:25,147 --> 00:34:26,482
Why did you kill him?

629
00:34:29,986 --> 00:34:31,028
Look at me.

630
00:34:33,114 --> 00:34:34,490
Why, Nathaniel?

631
00:34:36,576 --> 00:34:37,994
You seem like a good person.

632
00:34:39,328 --> 00:34:40,580
You come from good people.

633
00:34:42,874 --> 00:34:44,083
Why'd you kill him?

634
00:34:53,259 --> 00:34:54,385
Well, I'll be damned.

635
00:34:57,138 --> 00:34:58,598
That's your man, Agent Lisbon.

636
00:35:00,766 --> 00:35:01,809
That's your man.

637
00:35:15,128 --> 00:35:17,088
You had the evidence
against Winston Dellinger.

638
00:35:19,382 --> 00:35:20,425
I went to the lab.

639
00:35:21,218 --> 00:35:22,802
I swapped the blood sample
from his fender

640
00:35:22,928 --> 00:35:24,179
for another sample.

641
00:35:24,638 --> 00:35:25,680
Why'd you do it?

642
00:35:25,805 --> 00:35:27,140
I'm a silent partner in the bar.

643
00:35:28,391 --> 00:35:29,851
Everything I got is in that place.

644
00:35:30,352 --> 00:35:31,853
Last year, we got sued.

645
00:35:32,312 --> 00:35:34,814
- Guy got beat up in a fight.
- And the bar lost the suit?

646
00:35:35,190 --> 00:35:36,858
I was gonna lose
every penny I had.

647
00:35:38,109 --> 00:35:39,945
But when I caught
the Dellinger case

648
00:35:40,737 --> 00:35:43,490
I found out his father would hear
the appeal of the lawsuit.

649
00:35:43,740 --> 00:35:45,575
The judge must have been scared
about his son going to prison?

650
00:35:46,117 --> 00:35:47,661
Yeah. Terrified.

651
00:35:47,911 --> 00:35:49,829
I mean, he was sure
the kid would be killed

652
00:35:50,330 --> 00:35:52,040
'cause of all the guys
he put away.

653
00:35:52,874 --> 00:35:55,252
So I went to the judge
and made a deal.

654
00:35:56,044 --> 00:35:57,712
He'd rule in the bar's favor

655
00:35:57,921 --> 00:35:59,965
I'd hide the evidence
against Winston.

656
00:36:00,173 --> 00:36:01,550
How did that
get Winston killed?

657
00:36:02,008 --> 00:36:04,135
That night, I'm in bed, asleep.

658
00:36:04,928 --> 00:36:07,430
And Winston calls me
in a drunken panic.

659
00:36:07,847 --> 00:36:12,936
He says he was driving
and hit somebody... again.

660
00:36:13,228 --> 00:36:15,605
I said he should man up
and call the cops.

661
00:36:16,189 --> 00:36:19,025
He says if I don't help him

662
00:36:19,776 --> 00:36:21,903
he'll tell about the deal
I made with his father.

663
00:36:23,405 --> 00:36:25,782
I mean, he was gonna destroy
my career.

664
00:36:28,493 --> 00:36:30,078
"So I go out
to the place to meet him."

665
00:36:30,996 --> 00:36:32,622
"Look, I hit him right there."

666
00:36:33,623 --> 00:36:34,958
"Oh, my car."

667
00:36:36,084 --> 00:36:38,253
"Look, he must have crawled
off the road or some--"

668
00:36:39,963 --> 00:36:41,923
"Well, don't just stand there,
help me!"

669
00:36:42,132 --> 00:36:45,093
"You owe me! My dad saved your ass!
Now do something!"

670
00:36:46,469 --> 00:36:48,555
"He's freaking out. I mean,
he can't find the body."

671
00:36:49,598 --> 00:36:51,891
"He thinks maybe
whoever he hit"

672
00:36:52,017 --> 00:36:53,810
"is still alive
and crawled away."

673
00:36:54,394 --> 00:36:57,397
"I mean... he was outta control."

674
00:36:57,856 --> 00:36:59,399
"It's gotta be here somewhere."

675
00:37:00,108 --> 00:37:01,526
"And that's when I knew."

676
00:37:02,694 --> 00:37:04,070
"It's gotta be here."

677
00:37:04,404 --> 00:37:07,657
"If I don't do something
about this fool, right now..."

678
00:37:09,117 --> 00:37:10,160
"Winston."

679
00:37:10,327 --> 00:37:12,078
"He's gonna dog me
the rest of my life."

680
00:37:12,203 --> 00:37:13,246
"Sorry."

681
00:37:18,960 --> 00:37:21,296
You, uh, you ever find
the guy he hit?

682
00:37:22,964 --> 00:37:24,799
Must be still out there somewhere.

683
00:37:25,425 --> 00:37:26,468
No.

684
00:37:34,934 --> 00:37:36,770
But uniforms found a deer
that had been hit by a car

685
00:37:36,936 --> 00:37:38,063
a little ways off the road.

686
00:37:39,189 --> 00:37:40,690
Must have been too drunk
to know the difference.

687
00:37:41,066 --> 00:37:42,108
A deer?

688
00:37:45,695 --> 00:37:47,489
He hit a... a deer?

689
00:37:50,992 --> 00:37:52,035
That's perfect.

690
00:38:01,795 --> 00:38:03,588
So Minelli really hired
this Jane guy?

691
00:38:03,880 --> 00:38:06,383
Well, he exposed a corrupt cop
dethroned a judge.

692
00:38:06,716 --> 00:38:08,760
Those are all major points
for us.

693
00:38:09,928 --> 00:38:11,846
As far as Minelli's concerned,
he's a hero.

694
00:38:12,514 --> 00:38:13,556
And, uh...

695
00:38:14,683 --> 00:38:15,725
does Hannigan know about this?

696
00:38:15,892 --> 00:38:17,560
Yeah. He doesn't wanna work
with Jane

697
00:38:17,727 --> 00:38:19,187
so he's transferring
to another unit.

698
00:38:20,522 --> 00:38:21,773
Any idea who's gonna replace Hannigan?

699
00:38:22,065 --> 00:38:24,442
Don't know yet. There's a new class
of trainees coming up.

700
00:38:24,567 --> 00:38:25,610
Maybe we'll get one of them.

701
00:38:26,152 --> 00:38:27,445
Files are right there
if you wanna take a look.

702
00:38:33,702 --> 00:38:34,744
Like this one.

703
00:38:37,414 --> 00:38:39,624
She's cute. And outta your league.

704
00:38:42,502 --> 00:38:43,545
One last time--

705
00:38:44,045 --> 00:38:45,463
are you sure
you wanna do this?

706
00:38:46,172 --> 00:38:48,842
- Yes, I am.
- Okay. I tried.

707
00:38:50,051 --> 00:38:51,094
You did.

708
00:38:54,681 --> 00:38:55,724
Thank you.

709
00:39:05,525 --> 00:39:06,568
Shall we go?

710
00:39:15,243 --> 00:39:16,286
Here you go.

711
00:39:17,203 --> 00:39:19,873
I'm going home. If you need me
to explain anything, give me a call.

712
00:40:11,090 --> 00:40:12,133
Yes?

713
00:40:12,383 --> 00:40:13,426
"Virgil Minelli?"

714
00:40:14,886 --> 00:40:16,179
Yes. Who's this?

715
00:40:16,679 --> 00:40:18,723
Alexa Shultz, FBI.

716
00:40:18,848 --> 00:40:20,850
We met at the forensics conference
in Roanoke.

717
00:40:21,476 --> 00:40:24,813
Director Shultz.
What a pleasure to hear from you.

718
00:40:25,104 --> 00:40:27,732
I understand the CBI
has hired a new consultant.

719
00:40:28,149 --> 00:40:29,901
A man named Patrick Jane?

720
00:40:30,360 --> 00:40:31,402
"Yes."

721
00:40:32,028 --> 00:40:33,071
I'm surprised you know.

722
00:40:33,196 --> 00:40:35,657
I didn't realize you followed
our hiring that closely.

723
00:40:35,865 --> 00:40:38,576
Mr. Jane is connected
to a case we're interested in.

724
00:40:39,202 --> 00:40:40,954
The serial killer known
as Red John.

725
00:40:41,955 --> 00:40:44,624
"I'm, um, calling to ask a favor."

726
00:40:45,625 --> 00:40:46,668
What's that?

727
00:40:47,585 --> 00:40:51,047
I would appreciate updates
on the Red John case.

728
00:40:51,756 --> 00:40:54,384
"That way, when my boss
asks me what's going on"

729
00:40:54,509 --> 00:40:55,844
"I have something to tell him."

730
00:40:57,387 --> 00:40:58,972
To put it bluntly, Alexa

731
00:40:59,597 --> 00:41:00,682
why would I do that?

732
00:41:01,474 --> 00:41:02,517
"What's in it for me?"

733
00:41:02,851 --> 00:41:05,228
It's useful to have a friend
in the FBI, isn't it?

734
00:41:06,229 --> 00:41:07,730
"And I'm a good friend."

735
00:41:08,106 --> 00:41:13,027
Well, I'm a great believer
in inter-agency cooperation.

736
00:41:13,903 --> 00:41:16,281
"I don't see why
we couldn't engage in some."

737
00:41:17,365 --> 00:41:19,117
I look forward to it, Virgil.

738
00:41:19,742 --> 00:41:21,035
Oh, by the way

739
00:41:21,452 --> 00:41:24,372
one thing you might wanna know
about Patrick Jane--

740
00:41:25,456 --> 00:41:27,292
you know how he's been
outta sight in the past year?

741
00:41:27,834 --> 00:41:29,252
"You know where he's been?"

742
00:41:29,460 --> 00:41:30,503
No.

743
00:41:30,879 --> 00:41:32,130
An insane asylum.

744
00:41:33,256 --> 00:41:34,299
Good luck.

745
00:41:40,221 --> 00:41:41,264
Done.

746
00:41:43,641 --> 00:41:44,684
Thank you.

747
00:41:48,521 --> 00:41:49,564
Good morning.

748
00:42:17,467 --> 00:42:18,509
Hey, boss.

749
00:42:20,345 --> 00:42:21,429
We caught one. Fresno.

750
00:42:21,638 --> 00:42:23,389
Get Rigsby.
Let's leave before traffic.

751
00:42:23,556 --> 00:42:24,599
Okay.

